# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vouch - environment variables
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE
# 1. Make a copy of it and name the copy `.env.local`
#    (Mac/Linux terminal: cp .env.example .env.local)
# 2. Paste your real keys after each `=` sign. No quotes, no spaces.
# 3. Restart the dev server (Ctrl+C, then `npm run dev`) after any change.
#
# `.env.local` is ignored by git, so your keys never end up on GitHub.
# Full walkthrough of where each key comes from: see SETUP.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- STEP 1: Supabase (database, logins, resume storage) -- REQUIRED NOW ----
# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> Data API -> Project URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API Keys -> "Publishable" key
# (older projects call this the "anon public" key). Safe for the browser.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API Keys -> "Secret" key
# (older projects call this "service_role"). KEEP PRIVATE. Needed in Step 2.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# --- STEP 3: where the site lives ------------------------------------------
# Leave as-is while working on your laptop.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- STEP 4: Resend (sends the voucher's 6-digit verification email) --------
RESEND_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM=Vouch <onboarding@resend.dev>

# --- OPTIONAL: private test deployments ------------------------------------
# With no Resend key there is no inbox to check, so voucher codes can't be
# delivered. Set this to true on a PRIVATE test site to show the code on
# screen instead. Anyone who can see a code can verify as that person, so
# turn it off before sharing the site with anyone.
# SHOW_VERIFICATION_CODES=true

# --- STEP 8: Anthropic (reads resumes, scores candidate fit) ---------------
# console.anthropic.com -> API keys -> Create key. Starts with sk-ant-.
# OPTIONAL: without it, Vouch works exactly as before — resumes still upload,
# vouches still send, employers still hire. There are simply no AI scores.
# Costs a few cents per resume read and per candidate scored.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- STEP 9: Stripe (employer payments, voucher payouts) -------------------
# Stripe dashboard -> Developers -> API keys, with TEST MODE switched on.
# Test keys move no real money. KEEP THE SECRET KEY PRIVATE.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Stripe dashboard -> Developers -> Webhooks -> your endpoint -> signing secret.
# Starts whsec_. Without it, Vouch REFUSES incoming webhooks rather than
# trusting a call it cannot verify came from Stripe.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- STEP 9d: the nightly job ----------------------------------------------
# A long random password, yours to invent — 32+ characters of nonsense is
# ideal. It is what proves the nightly job at /api/cron/nightly was started by
# Vercel's scheduler and not by a stranger who guessed the address.
#
# Set it in VERCEL, not just here: Project -> Settings -> Environment
# Variables. Vercel then sends it on every scheduled call automatically, and
# there is nothing to configure on the cron entry itself.
#
# Without it the nightly sweeps refuse to run at all. That is deliberate — but
# it means payouts never become due and unanswered reports never become
# disputes, so this is not a key the live site can go without.
CRON_SECRET=

# --- STEP 9f: who may pay a voucher ----------------------------------------
# Your Supabase auth user ID. NOT your email: a logged-in person can rewrite
# their own email column in the database (proven, not assumed), so an email
# list here would be a promotion anybody could grant themselves in one update.
#
# You do not have to go looking for it. Sign in, visit /admin/payouts, and the
# page shows you your own ID to copy — because until this is set, nobody is an
# admin and that screen grants nothing.
#
# Set it in VERCEL and redeploy. Several admins: separate with commas.
ADMIN_USER_IDS=
